            "instrument": "python_module",
            "label": "compiled arm authority and pulse response",
            "module": "robot_learning.lab.arm_authority"
          }
        ],
        "rationale": "The consequential initial distinction is whether the exact compiled motor authority and damping have a usable local timescale from the singular reset and representative reachable postures, or whether effort/settling constraints should shape controller development before a training-only intervention. No candidate or completed training exists, and unchanged PPO training covers only 14-20 cm of the official 6-20 cm radius range, so candidate selection cannot answer this question and training immediately would leave a known distribution confound. The PI-owned diagnostic measures compiled inertia and actual direct bounded-command response at reset plus both elbow branches for 6, 13, and 20 cm targets; its 20 ms pulse timing matches the official control interval. Results can justify prioritizing trajectory/braking research if authority or decay is consequentially slow, or support proceeding to full-distribution learned-policy development if local authority is not a plausible limiting mechanism. This probe does not establish closed-loop target-reaching, hold performance, candidate runtime semantics, bearing coverage, or protected substep checking; those remain for later policy evaluation and targeted investigation."
      },
